Note: You had to have some kind of a bug in the production code for Pex to create a test (assume in this case). Pex uses path condition analysis to generate different code paths and execute tests based on those paths. If it doesn't find a path condition that is true, the test runs only the initial path and it cannot generate the test at all.

Finally, always keep in mind that the Pex tool only looks for the paths in the current 'state' of the code and it does not analyze the execution or the history of past executions.

